---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend';
const title = 'Yotpo Email & SMS vs Omnisend for Shopify: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Yotpo Email & SMS is retired. Rebuild multichannel recovery without assuming channel permissions transfer.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I choose Yotpo Email & SMS today?",
    "answer": "Yotpo states that the application is decommissioned. This is now a migration decision, separate from retaining its Reviews or Loyalty products."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will Omnisend recreate my old signup forms?",
    "answer": "Its migration guide describes manual rebuilding or its migration service. Validate targeting, consent wording and discount behavior after rebuilding."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does importing email contacts restore push reach?",
    "answer": "Do not treat an email import as a push subscription. Check browser eligibility and channel permissions separately before enabling push branches."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I test replenishment?",
    "answer": "Use representative products and bundles with different usage patterns. Verify item data, purchase exits and permission checks before choosing a cadence; the scenario is a proposed acceptance test."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I export from the retired account now?",
    "answer": "Do not assume access remains available. Use records already retained and ask the relevant support teams about missing data; this page promises no recovery or export access."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I also evaluate Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "You can include Sequenzy in the email shortlist. Verify the required Shopify events, suppression, consent handling and current commercial terms before choosing it; it is not assumed to replace SMS or review infrastructure."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-cyan-100/90">/</span>
        <span class="text-cyan-100/90">Yotpo Email & SMS vs Omnisend</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="badge">Migration comparison · reviewed November 24, 2026</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS vs Omnisend for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Rebuild multichannel recovery without assuming channel permissions transfer. Yotpo confirms that Email &amp; SMS has been decommissioned. This page evaluates a replacement workflow, not a trial of two currently available senders.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Map the migration before enabling presets</h2>
        <p>Omnisend publishes a Yotpo migration guide covering contacts, signup forms and messaging setup. Treat that guide as a mapping reference, not proof that a retired Yotpo account can still export data. Locate the files and permission records you already possess; ask support about gaps without promising that missing records can be recovered.</p>
        <h2>Email, SMS and push require separate routing</h2>
        <p>Omnisend documents email, SMS and web push. An imported email address does not establish SMS permission or a working browser push subscription. Build a channel eligibility map before restoring a multichannel journey. If a channel is unavailable, define whether the journey waits, ends or takes a permitted alternative rather than blindly sending the next touch.</p>
        <h2>Proposed streetwear drop scenario</h2>
        <p>For a hypothetical streetwear release, stage a customer who has email permission but no SMS permission, a browser with push enabled, and a recent purchaser. Check the permitted branch for each and ensure a purchase removes the customer from recovery before another reminder. Browser and device reach should be observed in a controlled check; mobile traffic alone is not evidence that push can reach that shopper.</p>
        <h2>Welcome forms and incentives must be rebuilt together</h2>
        <p>The migration guide says forms must be recreated manually or through its migration service. Reproduce the intended audience and offer rules, not just the visual design. Test a returning subscriber, an existing customer and a new subscriber so an import or resubmission does not issue an unintended second welcome discount.</p>
        <h2>Keep reviews and loyalty ownership explicit</h2>
        <p>Keeping Yotpo Reviews does not make the retired messaging suite available. Decide which remaining service sends review requests and reward notifications, then exclude duplicate invitations from new post-purchase flows. If candle scent preferences or tea bundle contents should affect replenishment, inspect the product data received rather than using a single reorder delay for every purchase.</p>
        <h2>Compare reachable demand and total cost</h2>
        <p>Quote contacts and expected sends separately from SMS usage and any retained review or loyalty subscription. Push is an additional channel to evaluate, not evidence of free incremental recovery. Compare completed purchases, discounts, unsubscribe behavior and message costs with a clearly defined attribution window; a dashboard credit is not proof that a push reminder caused an order.</p>
        <h2>Where Sequenzy fits</h2>
        <p>If you are considering Sequenzy for email, compare the same required events, exclusions and operating tasks before selecting it. Confirm current Shopify integration scope and pricing directly. Do not assume it replaces the SMS sender, review collection or loyalty service.</p>
        <h2>Primary evidence and limits</h2>
        <p>Supplier documentation checked November 24, 2026. No live migration, deliverability experiment or merchant revenue test was performed. Current account eligibility, quotes and missing historical records remain to be confirmed.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo decommissioning notice</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/12048785-migrate-from-yotpo-to-omnisend">Omnisend Yotpo migration guide</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/8172193-get-started-with-omnisend">Omnisend channel overview</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Omnisend vs Yotpo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-klaviyo">Yotpo vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-omnisend">Sequenzy vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/reviews-and-ugc">Reviews & UGC playbook</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/home-goods">Email apps for home goods stores</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Yotpo Email &amp; SMS vs Omnisend FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
